          "git_sha": "23bce6e2a2e83612581f9eb7f838f78121e5d17f",
          "line_end": 116,
          "line_start": 115,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "vercel-labs/deepsec",
          "url": "https://github.com/vercel-labs/deepsec/blob/23a69227e3380e6b44a7ebd93c52e023c59f17c3/README.md#L115-L116"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_7c425deefe2257248f205ce7fdd9d3b134151ee343ca6307825b9b0e32923f8c",
        "slc_9b636c7cea04169614e89455ee4e95753cb6e4a7ab5eeb8123805b22f9825f6c"
      ],
      "text": "The security model treats deepsec like a coding agent with full shell access on its host environment; in sandbox mode, agent API keys are injected outside the sandbox and worker egress is limited to coding-agent hosts."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_b37ec0fefb68564ecfa35c738009ab786ebd3dad642e86daf6f01dc594b706e8",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "dependencies",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "23a69227e3380e6b44a7ebd93c52e023c59f17c3",
          "git_sha": "23bce6e2a2e83612581f9eb7f838f78121e5d17f",
          "line_end": 87,
          "line_start": 79,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "vercel-labs/deepsec",
          "url": "https://github.com/vercel-labs/deepsec/blob/23a69227e3380e6b44a7ebd93c52e023c59f17c3/README.md#L79-L87"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_0f51d16662ac36553c8b53740e3feeb0d76c95535cdbc22cfee6af829ccabb96"
      ],
      "text": "By default model calls route through Vercel AI Gateway; users can instead bring their own OpenAI, Anthropic, or custom HTTPS provider key via --model-auth direct with --ai-provider and --ai-api-key-env."
    },
